      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of guilt toward your own ceilings is dangerous because it blurs the line between societal expectations and your true potential. Often, the most impactful people are those who redefine \"significance\" not by climbing existing ladders, but by building new paths that others didn't knowneeded. If you stop viewing your average math skills as a limitation and start seeing them as a foundation for a personal legacy, the difference between \"existing\" and \"making things\" becomes much less apparent.",
      "source": "target",
